WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.370
The first answer is,

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:06.260
by storing the result of a ko.observableArray() to a variable.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.600
And just like observables,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.280
you have the option of passing in a normal array as the initial state.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.720
And the answer to the second question is, by just calling the array methods,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.420
like pop() and push(), directly on the observable array.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.430
The developers of Knockout have made this very easy.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:27.430
You can treat observable arrays almost the same as you treat normal arrays,

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.630
with the primary exception being how you retrieve values.

